<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajasthan High Court</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> High Court is the high court of the Indian state of Rajasthan, inaugurated in August 1949 with its principal seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a>, a location chosen to balance Jodhpur against the state capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaipur">Jaipur</a>. It replaced the separate high courts of the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a>, and a permanent bench also sits at Jaipur.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajasthan-high-court.jpg" alt="Rajasthan High Court" width="320" height="164" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TrendSPLEND · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Rajasthan_High_Court_Building.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
